gaJr(){return"Return per unit of risk, after subtracting the risk-free rate.\n\n< 0 \u2014 Losing to the risk-free rate\n0\u20131 \u2014 Suboptimal risk/reward\n1\u20132 \u2014 Good\n> 2  \u2014 Excellent\n\nHigher is better. A Sharpe of 1.0 means you're earning 1% of excess return per 1% of volatility, annualised.\n\nDisplayed as \u2014 when fewer than 5 observations or volatility is near-zero, as the ratio is statistically unreliable in those cases."},
